{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"9c7802a2a5aebab6","type":"text","text":"**Rules types in Data Quality Rules.**\nThere may be many rule type in DQ rules among them below are some of the important rules which we are going to implement.\n\n\n1. conditional_constraints(HIGHEST) : \n\t1. Business logic dependencies between fields.\n\t2. Rules where one field's values determines requirement for other fields.\n\t3. Example \"if status = completed\" then completion date is required\n2. referential(HIGH) :\n\t1. relationship consistency between tables.\n\t2. validates foreign key relationships and cross-table references.\n\t3. Example customer_id exists in customer table, valid category references\n3. Integrity(HIGH) :\n\t1. Data format and structural correctness\n\t2. Examples: email format validation, phone number patterns, date formats\n4. completeness(MEDIUM) :\n\t1. Required field validation\n\t2. checks that mandatory fields contain values\n\t3. Example customer name is mandatory in customer table\n5. uniqueness (MEDIUM) : \n\t1. Prevents data duplication issues.\n\t2. Example no duplicate serial numbers should be present in a table\n\nSo about business rules as rule_type is not actually a rule type rather both are from different layers, LLM may have hallucinated and returned the result as business rules, even the system prompt doesnt contain the term called \"business rules\" in rule_type.","x":-580,"y":-180,"width":1000,"height":940},
		{"id":"3c8b77de8cf8c6db","type":"text","text":"Code Alignments.\n\n1. Before the script was independent, now script have been exposed  to fastapi\n2. Exposed endpoint in the same way as we did for three stages, here the stage is (bronze_validation)\n3. As of now there are four prompts\n\t1. system prompt - defines the tasks to LLM\n\t2. context prompt - input for the LLM\n\t3. user prompt - send source name and batch number to the LLM\n\t4. external context - external context given by the user.\n4. for source level scope  \n\t1. generating source level rules the system prompt is hard-coded (line number 388)\n\t2. here the external context is passed to the function but not to the LLM.\n5. Not sure the llm call is made during the table rules generation.(line number 333)\n\t1. By observing the column rules generation function we can see the prompt that defines the table generation.(line 173)\n6. for column level scope the inputs are system prompt, context prompt, user prompt\n\t1. here inputs passed to the llm are functions defined in the code itself.\n7. **Need Clarification on inputs for passing to the LLM.**\n8. Made Configure driven code.(added configuration in the config.py file)\n9. Used utils function for externalising.","x":-1640,"y":2120,"width":1320,"height":680},
		{"id":"a5aaf65470014a80","type":"text","text":"```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Start([validation_main]) --> LoadConfig[load_config: Load validation config]\n    LoadConfig --> InitGenerator[ValidationRuleGenerator.__init__: Initialize generator]\n    \n    InitGenerator --> InitConcurrency[_initialize_concurrency_controls: Setup semaphores & batch size]\n    InitGenerator --> InitDB[_initialize_database_connections: Connect to MongoDB]\n    InitGenerator --> InitLLM[_initialize_llm: Setup Azure OpenAI]\n    \n    InitLLM --> RunValidation[run_validation_generation: Entry point for generation]\n    RunValidation --> LoadPrompt[load_prompt: Load system prompt]\n    LoadPrompt --> GenerateParallel[generate_validation_rules_parallel: Main orchestrator]\n    \n    GenerateParallel --> GetSources[get_all_sources: Fetch all sources from MongoDB]\n    GetSources --> ProcessSourcesParallel{Process sources in parallel}\n    \n    ProcessSourcesParallel --> ProcessSource[_process_source: Process single source]\n    \n    ProcessSource --> GetTables[_get_tables_for_source: Fetch tables with caching]\n    ProcessSource --> GetContext[_get_external_context: Fetch business context]\n    \n    GetTables --> ProcessTablesParallel{Process tables in parallel}\n    ProcessTablesParallel --> ProcessTable[_process_table: Process single table]\n    \n    ProcessTable --> GetColumns[_get_columns_for_table: Fetch columns with caching]\n    GetColumns --> BatchColumns[Create column batches based on COLUMN_BATCH_SIZE]\n    \n    BatchColumns --> ProcessBatchesParallel{Process column batches in parallel}\n    ProcessBatchesParallel --> ProcessBatch[_process_column_batch: Process column batch]\n    \n    ProcessBatch --> PrepareContext1[_prepare_context_prompt: Build context string]\n    ProcessBatch --> PrepareUser1[_prepare_user_prompt: Build user prompt]\n    PrepareUser1 --> QueryLLM1[_query_llm_with_retry: Call Azure OpenAI]\n    \n    QueryLLM1 --> ParseRules1[_parse_and_format_rules: Parse LLM response]\n    \n    ParseRules1 --> BuildLookups1[_build_lookup_maps: Create ID mappings]\n    BuildLookups1 --> ResolveIDs1[_resolve_ids: Map names to IDs by scope]\n    ResolveIDs1 --> FormatRules1[Format validation rules with proper IDs]\n    \n    FormatRules1 --> CollectTableRules[Collect all table rules]\n    \n    ProcessTable --> CollectTableRules\n    \n    GetContext --> GenerateSourceRules[_generate_source_level_rules: Cross-table rules]\n    \n    GenerateSourceRules --> PrepareSourceContext[Prepare source context prompt]\n    PrepareSourceContext --> QueryLLM2[_query_llm_with_retry: Call Azure OpenAI]\n    QueryLLM2 --> ParseRules2[_parse_and_format_rules: Parse source rules]\n    \n    ParseRules2 --> BuildLookups2[_build_lookup_maps: Create ID mappings]\n    BuildLookups2 --> ResolveIDs2[_resolve_ids: Map names to IDs]\n    ResolveIDs2 --> FormatRules2[Format source-level validation rules]\n    \n    CollectTableRules --> CombineRules[Combine all rules: column + table + source]\n    FormatRules2 --> CombineRules\n    \n    CombineRules --> StoreRules[_store_validation_rules: Batch insert to MongoDB]\n    \n    StoreRules --> UpdateStatus[Update source processing status]\n    UpdateStatus --> NextSource{More sources?}\n    \n    NextSource -->|Yes| ProcessSource\n    NextSource -->|No| AggregateResults[Aggregate all source results]\n    \n    AggregateResults --> ReturnStatus[Return overall status report]\n    ReturnStatus --> PrintResults[Print results to console]\n    PrintResults --> CloseConnections[close_connections: Close MongoDB]\n    CloseConnections --> End([End])\n    \n    style Start fill:#e1f5e1\n    style End fill:#ffe1e1\n    style GenerateParallel fill:#fff4e6\n    style ProcessSourcesParallel fill:#e6f3ff\n    style ProcessTablesParallel fill:#e6f3ff\n    style ProcessBatchesParallel fill:#e6f3ff\n    style QueryLLM1 fill:#ffe6f0\n    style QueryLLM2 fill:#ffe6f0\n    style StoreRules fill:#f0e6ff\n```\n","x":3,"y":2360,"width":1477,"height":4660},
		{"id":"4d0f4b04327f7e20","type":"text","text":"**Development Plan:**\n\nStep 1: Extract Metadata\nStep 2: Build a query to get the external context by making an LLM call.\nStep 3: Load the prompts\n\tPrompts contains:\n\t1. System prompt\n\t2. User prompt\n\t3. external context\nStep 4: Make the LLM calls for generating the rules for all the three of them(source, table and column)\nStep 5: Parse the LLM response\nStep 6: Store the result to mongodb. ","x":1540,"y":780,"width":1140,"height":580},
		{"id":"8fd034c1ca3c806d","type":"text","text":"```json\n# source sample metadata\n{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"id\": \"s_crm\",\n    \"label\": \"CRM\",\n    \"be_name\": \"CRM\",\n    \"type\": \"source\",\n    \"description\": \"This data source serves as a placeholder for future data integration and analysis.\"\n  },\n  \"embedding_input\": \"This source represents a foundational element within the organization's data architecture, designed to accommodate future data tables and integration processes. Although currently devoid of any tables, it is intended to support critical business operations by providing a structured environment for data collection, analysis, and reporting. The absence of tables indicates that this source is in a preliminary stage, potentially awaiting the integration of various data entities that will facilitate decision-making workflows and analytical requirements. As the organization evolves, this source will play a pivotal role in consolidating data from various business processes, ensuring that relevant information is accessible for semantic search and discovery. The future tables associated with this source will likely encompass key data entities that align with the organization's strategic objectives, thereby enhancing the overall data ecosystem.\",\n  \"tables\": [\n    \"contributiontransactionlink\",\n    \"promoquarterly\",\n    \"_17_18to24_25packagesv2\",\n    \"appealsourcestructure05_06_25\",\n    \"dimconstituents_anon_\",\n    \"productionseason_types\",\n    \"batchsummary\",\n    \"deferralsandreceiveablesnotinmodelyet\",\n    \"ticketf\",\n    \"_1824funds\",\n    \"_1824members2\",\n    \"ticketseatid\",\n    \"deceasedcontwlastactivity5_1_25\",\n    \"conttypes_afasa1a2relationships\",\n    \"contributionoutputv2\"\n  ],\n  \"embedding_vector\": [\n    -0.021939603611826897,\n    -0.010890079662203789,\n    ......\n    ]\n    }\n```\n\n```json\n# table sample metadata\n{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"id\": \"534ead1b0043932ee1ebb401081f334d\",\n    \"icon\": \"\",\n    \"label\": \"Contribution Transaction Link\",\n    \"be_name\": \"contributiontransactionlink\",\n    \"type\": \"table\",\n    \"parent_type\": \"source\",\n    \"parent_id\": \"s_crm\",\n    \"parent_name\": \"CRM\",\n    \"count\": 16,\n    \"description\": \"Links contribution transactions within the CRM system.\",\n    \"columns\": [\n      \"days_in_date\",\n      \"gl_account\",\n      \"mode_of_sale_category\",\n      \"mode_of_sale\",\n      \"sales_channel\",\n      \"debit_amount\",\n      \"credit_amount\",\n      \"transaction_category\",\n      \"fund_id\",\n      \"campaign_id\",\n      \"transaction_type\",\n      \"transaction_amount\",\n      \"gl_entry_type\",\n      \"batch_id\",\n      \"transaction_id\",\n      \"contribution_id\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"embedding_input\": \"The Contribution Transaction Link table serves as a pivotal component in the CRM data architecture, designed to capture and manage the relationships between various contribution transactions. This table is essential for supporting critical business operations related to financial contributions, enabling detailed analysis and reporting on transaction activities. It encompasses key identifiers such as transaction_id, which serves as the primary key, and various attributes that detail the nature of each transaction, including contribution_id, batch_id, transaction_amount, and associated campaign and fund identifiers. The table is structured to facilitate efficient data retrieval and integration with other business processes, ensuring that relevant information is readily accessible for decision-making workflows. As the organization evolves, this table will play a crucial role in consolidating data from diverse sources, thereby enhancing the overall data ecosystem and supporting analytical requirements. The data lifecycle for this table includes regular updates aligned with transaction processing, ensuring data quality and compliance with financial reporting standards.\",\n  \"tags\": [\n    \"CRM\",\n    \"Contribution\",\n    \"Transaction\"\n  ],\n  \"primary_keys\": [\n    \"transaction_id\"\n  ],\n  \"foreign_keys\": [\n    \"customer_no\",\n    \"promotion_appeal\",\n    \"user_id\",\n    \"event_bundle_sequence_id\",\n    \"pseudo_user_id\",\n    \"batch_id\"\n  ],\n  \"foreign_keys_referencing_tables\": [\n    {\n      \"target_table_name\": \"Contact Types Relationships\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"customer_no\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Links customer contributions to their respective types and relationships within the CRM system.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"many-to-one\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_table_name\": \"Promo Quarterly\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"promotion_appeal\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Associates contributions with specific promotional campaigns and their responses.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"many-to-one\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_table_name\": \"batch summary\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"batch_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Links contribution transactions to their respective batch summaries for processing insights.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"many-to-one\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_table_name\": \"users\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"user_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Connects contributions to the users who processed or managed the transactions.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"many-to-one\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_table_name\": \"pseudonymous users\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"pseudo_user_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Links contributions to pseudonymous user interactions within the CRM system.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"many-to-one\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_table_name\": \"Deferrals and Receiveables Not in Model Yet\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"batch_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Associates contributions with deferrals and receivables awaiting modeling.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"many-to-one\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"target_table_name\": \"Deferrals and Receiveables Not in Model Yet\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"transaction_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"References Deferrals and Receiveables Not in Model Yet: This table links contribution transactions, referencing the transaction_id from the target table.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"many-to-one\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"primary_keys_referencing_tables\": [\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"Contribution Output\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"contribution_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Links contribution transactions to their respective output details for analysis.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"one-to-many\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"Ticket\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"ticket_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Associates ticket sales with contribution transactions for campaign analysis.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"one-to-many\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"Packages\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"transaction_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Referenced by Packages: Packages may be linked to specific contribution transactions.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"one-to-many\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"Appeal Source Structure\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"transaction_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Referenced by Appeal Source Structure: Appeal sources may be associated with specific contribution transactions.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"one-to-many\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"production season types\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"transaction_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Referenced by production season types: The production season types may relate to contribution transactions, indicating how seasonal productions impact financial contributions.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"one-to-many\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"batch summary\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"transaction_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Referenced by batch summary: Each batch summary may encompass multiple transactions linked to contributions processed in that batch.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"one-to-many\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"Ticket\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"transaction_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Referenced by Ticket: Each ticket may be linked to a specific transaction for tracking sales.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"one-to-many\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"Funds\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"contribution_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Referenced by Funds: Links contributions to specific funds for financial tracking and reporting.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"one-to-many\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"members\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"contribution_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Referenced by members: Links contributions made by members to their respective transactions.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"one-to-many\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"Ticket Seat ID\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"transaction_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Referenced by Ticket Seat ID: The ticket seat may be linked to a specific transaction, providing financial context to ticket sales.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"one-to-many\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"to_table\": \"Contribution Output\",\n      \"linking_column\": \"transaction_id\",\n      \"relation_description\": \"Referenced by Contribution Output: Links contribution transactions to their respective contributions for detailed financial analysis.\",\n      \"relationship\": \"one-to-many\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_by\": \"demo_user\",\n  \"created_at\": {\n    \"$date\": \"2025-08-13T13:59:43.905Z\"\n  },\n  \"last_updated_by\": \"relationship_inference\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2025-09-19T12:21:47.997939Z\",\n  \"human_feedback\": [\n    {\n      \"user\": \"\",\n      \"comment\": \"\",\n      \"timestamp\": \"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"embedding_vector\": [\n    -0.016587408259510994,\n    -0.018524399027228355,\n    ....\n    ]\n    }\n```\n\n```json\n# column metadata\n{\n  \"data\": {\n    \"id\": \"e8f08a6c21e1ae5c8e261207c9045082\",\n    \"label\": \"constituent_id\",\n    \"be_name\": \"constituent_id\",\n    \"type\": \"column\",\n    \"data_type\": \"integer\",\n    \"nullable\": \"true\",\n    \"parent_type\": \"table\",\n    \"parent_id\": \"34aff2970f6552ee316eb546c6c258ca\",\n    \"parent_name\": \"Packages\",\n    \"description\": \"Identifier for the constituent associated with the package.\"\n  },\n  \"embedding_input\": \"The constituent_id column is an integer field that serves as an identifier for the constituent linked to the package. It is nullable, indicating that there may be instances where a package is not directly associated with a specific constituent. This column is essential for establishing relationships with other entities within the CRM, particularly in contexts where package details are analyzed in relation to constituent data. It is expected to be used in joins and filters when querying package information alongside constituent records.\",\n  \"sample_values\": [],\n  \"tags\": [\n    \"Constituent\",\n    \"Identifier\",\n    \"CRM\"\n  ],\n  \"created_by\": \"demo_user\",\n  \"created_at\": {\n    \"$date\": \"2025-08-13T13:59:43.905Z\"\n  },\n  \"last_updated_by\": \"user_ai\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2025-09-19T12:16:46.528948Z\",\n  \"human_feedback\": [\n    {\n      \"user\": \"\",\n      \"comment\": \"\",\n      \"timestamp\": \"\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"embedding_vector\": [\n    0.0005872722831554711,\n    0.0023115037474781275,\n    ]\n    }\n```\n","x":3000,"y":780,"width":880,"height":580},
		{"id":"d683de4398cf5eb0","type":"text","text":"```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant App as Your Application\n    participant LLM as Azure OpenAI LLM\n    participant Search as Azure Cognitive Search\n    participant DB as MongoDB\n\n    Note over App: Start CDC / Metadata Task\n    App->>App: Split work into tasks (tables/columns)\n    App->>App: Acquire table_semaphore (limits tables in parallel)\n\n    par Parallel Task Execution\n        App->>App: Acquire llm_semaphore (limits LLM calls)\n        App->>Search: Vector Search Query\n        Search-->>App: Top N Chunks (context)\n        App->>LLM: Send Prompt + Context\n        LLM-->>App: Enriched Metadata\n        App->>DB: Update table/column metadata\n        App->>App: Release llm_semaphore\n    and\n        App->>App: Acquire llm_semaphore (another parallel task)\n        App->>Search: Vector Search Query\n        Search-->>App: Top N Chunks (context)\n        App->>LLM: Send Prompt + Context\n        LLM-->>App: Enriched Metadata\n        App->>DB: Update table/column metadata\n        App->>App: Release llm_semaphore\n    end\n\n    App->>App: Release table_semaphore (when table finished)\n    Note over App: All tasks done → pipeline complete\n\n```\n\n","x":3360,"y":2440,"width":1000,"height":1520},
		{"id":"622974c4023cf731","type":"text","text":"```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    %% Day 1: Initial Rule Generation\n    A[Day 1 Sources] --> B[Generate Business Rules]\n    B --> C[Store Rules in MongoDB]\n    C --> D[Generate Embeddings for Rules]\n    D --> E[Store Rule Embeddings in Vector Store]\n    \n    %% Stored Data\n    subgraph \"Stored Data\"\n        C1[MongoDB: Rule Docs]\n        E1[Vector Store: Rule Embeddings and Metadata]\n    end\n    C --> C1\n    E --> E1\n    \n    %% Day 2: New Sources\n    F[Day 2 Sources] --> G[Generate Table and Column Embeddings - optional]\n    G --> H[Query Day 1 Vector Store for Relevant Rules]\n    E1 --> H\n    H --> I[Send Relevant Day 1 Rules plus Day 2 Schema to LLM]\n    I --> J[Generate Day 2 Rules]\n    \n    %% Store New Rules\n    J --> K[Store Day 2 Rules in MongoDB]\n    K --> L[Generate Embeddings for Day 2 Rules]\n    L --> M[Update Vector Store with Day 2 Rule Embeddings]\n    \n    %% Stored Data\n    K --> C1\n    M --> E1\n    \n    %% Styling\n    classDef storage fill:#f9f,stroke:#333,stroke-width:1px,color:#000\n    class C1,E1 storage\n```\n\n","x":4516,"y":2609,"width":884,"height":1511}
	],
	"edges":[]
}